  "tagline": "Google's original small, fast LSM key-value library, now in limited-maintenance mode.",
  "description": "LevelDB is the compact C++ library Jeff Dean and Sanjay Ghemawat released in 2011, bringing Bigtable's SSTable and LSM ideas to a single-process embeddable store. It provides an ordered map of byte-string keys to values with snapshots, atomic batches and Snappy compression, and it still sits inside Chrome's IndexedDB implementation and Bitcoin Core's chainstate. The repository is explicitly in very limited maintenance and the last tagged release was 1.23 in 2021. For new work, RocksDB, Pebble or a Rust engine offer more features and active development; LevelDB remains a readable reference implementation.",
